    "methodology_summary": "The authors apply three machine learning classifiers (k-Nearest Neighbors, Random Forest, and eXtreme Gradient Boosting) to predict the next 4-hour market direction (up or down) of three cryptocurrency pairs (ETH-USDT, LTC-BTC, and ZEC-BTC). The feature space consists of the previous 60 periods of OHLCV data, tested both with and without technical indicators (such as CCI, RSI, DMI, MACD, and Bollinger Bands) added via feature augmentation. A strategy is constructed by taking long/flat positions based on whether the predicted price movement exceeds the exchange's trading fee threshold, evaluated on an out-of-sample 5% test span (approximately 66 days).",
